    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 4th slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups against high-xERA arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) is our premier start, leveraging his leadoff spot against Kyle Leahy and a significant platoon edge that boosts his projected output by 14%. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (74.32) is positioned for a high-ceiling outing against Merrill Kelly; despite a minor BvP concern, the combination of his leadoff role and the exploitable 5.47 xERA of the opposing starter makes him an essential fixture in today\u2019s outfield. We are also leaning heavily into **Trea Turner** (67.05) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.71), whose high-leverage positions and consistent contact profiles against Michael Wacha provide a reliable foundation for our daily efficiency target.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the marginal utility of our bench depth against the current starting configuration. **Josh Smith** (57.16) was the most difficult exclusion, finishing just behind **Luke Raley** (58.59). While **Josh Smith** benefits from a strong platoon edge against Jack Flaherty, the optimizer favored **Luke Raley** due to the favorable 5.52 xERA presented by Shane Bieber. Meanwhile, **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) warrants a mention for his surprising efficiency today; an advantageous park factor and a robust 11% platoon bump push him into \"Strong\" territory. It is vital to note that all lineup slots are currently based on projected batting orders; should lineups shuffle before first pitch, particularly for **Gary Sanchez** or **Dillon Dingler**, the resulting changes in their order-based score modifiers could necessitate further adjustments to our strategy to protect our game caps.",
